/* Region — a run of 64-bit words the operating system gave, owned by whoever
 * asked SystemOs for it. The handle is opaque: no fun here reads or writes its
 * words, and no literal is a region. A heap that lives in a region reads and
 * writes its words through faces of its own house; everyone else holds the
 * handle and gives it back with SystemOs.unmap. */
place Region is internal i64 {
}
